{"team":"ARI","col":"#E64868","identity":"balanced","funnel":"run-funnel","plays_pg":61.9,"adot":7.0,"report_html":"<div class=\"report\"><h2>Matchup-Driven</h2><p><strong>Trey McBride</strong> is a genuine centerpiece, not an afterthought \u2014 <strong>28%</strong> of targets (league ~15%).</p><h3>The Offensive Blueprint</h3><p>There's no bell-cow to bank on \u2014 the lead back sees just <strong>49%</strong> of carries (league ~59%), a committee that caps any one back's ceiling and makes their rushing props matchup- and script-dependent.</p><p>ARI throw by design. They pass <strong>+1%</strong> over expectation (league -2%) and keep firing even with a lead (45% early-down pass when ahead vs ~41%) \u2014 the kind of pass-first identity that keeps receivers live in every script.</p><p>When they fall behind they abandon the run entirely \u2014 64% pass while trailing, so their pass-catchers have huge comeback-script ceilings.</p><h3>In the Red Zone</h3><p>Inside the 20 they stay aggressive, throwing <strong>59%</strong> of the time, which puts scoring equity on <strong>Michael Wilson</strong>. And with the TE commanding 28% of targets, <strong>Trey McBride</strong> is a live red-zone option too.</p><h2>Defense \u2014 The Run Comes Free</h2><p>They surrender <strong>128 rushing</strong> and <strong>237 passing</strong> yards per game (league ~120 / ~230). The run moves against them \u2014 <strong>target opposing RB1s</strong>.</p><p><strong>Soft against backs out of the backfield</strong> \u2014 23 rec yds/game (vs ~18). A rec-yards target.</p><p>They lock down opposing WR2s \u2014 just 30 rec yds/game (vs ~36); fade receiving props there.</p><p>Broadly a leaky unit \u2014 48% success rate allowed (vs ~44%); points come easy against them.</p><p>They leak <strong>WR1 receiving TDs</strong> (0.47/game vs ~0.38) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><p>They leak <strong>TE touchdowns</strong> (0.32/game vs ~0.24) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><h2>The Betting Angles</h2><p>Bottom line: their pass-catchers have massive ceilings in comeback scripts (fade-material as underdogs); <strong>opposing RB1s</strong> smash on the ground and at the goal line; <strong>opposing TE anytime-TD</strong> is a repeatable angle.</p><p><em>Built on 2024\u201325 data; the profile rebuilds through the season as the current staff and roster set their own tendencies.</em></p></div>","depth":{"QB":[{"name":"Jacoby Brissett","slot":"QB1","starter":true,"td":9,"props":{"Comp":23.33,"Att":36.28,"Pass Yds":240.0,"Pass TD":1.34,"INT":0.45,"Rush Yds":14.15},"d":{"completions":23.33,"attempts":36.28,"pass_yards":240.0,"pass_td":1.34,"interceptions":0.45,"rush_att":3.06,"rush_yards":14.15}}],"RB":[{"name":"Jeremiyah Love","slot":"RB1","starter":true,"td":29,"props":{"Rush Att":16.9,"Rush Yds":72.43,"Tgt":3.17,"Rec":2.51,"Rec Yds":19.21},"d":{"rush_att":16.9,"rush_yards":72.43,"targets":3.17,"receptions":2.51,"rec_yards":19.21,"rec_td":0.07}},{"name":"Tyler Allgeier","slot":"RB2","starter":true,"td":23,"props":{"Rush Att":9.29,"Rush Yds":38.61,"Tgt":2.55,"Rec":1.84,"Rec Yds":14.36},"d":{"rush_att":9.29,"rush_yards":38.61,"targets":2.55,"receptions":1.84,"rec_yards":14.36,"rec_td":0.05}},{"name":"Bam Knight","slot":"RB3","starter":false,"td":27,"props":{"Rush Att":9.79,"Rush Yds":34.66,"Tgt":4.35,"Rec":2.94,"Rec Yds":21.3},"d":{"rush_att":9.79,"rush_yards":34.66,"targets":4.35,"receptions":2.94,"rec_yards":21.3,"rec_td":0.07}}],"WR":[{"name":"Marvin Harrison Jr.","slot":"WR1","starter":true,"td":27,"props":{"Tgt":7.34,"Rec":4.18,"Rec Yds":59.27,"Rec TD":0.31},"d":{"targets":7.34,"receptions":4.18,"rec_yards":59.27,"rec_td":0.31}},{"name":"Michael Wilson","slot":"WR2","starter":true,"td":33,"props":{"Tgt":9.92,"Rec":6.46,"Rec Yds":83.16,"Rec TD":0.38},"d":{"targets":9.92,"receptions":6.46,"rec_yards":83.16,"rec_td":0.38}},{"name":"Kendrick Bourne","slot":"WR3","starter":true,"td":13,"props":{"Tgt":4.1,"Rec":2.53,"Rec Yds":31.68,"Rec TD":0.14},"d":{"targets